00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:55.490
Of any moment on The Office, that is, like, my best moment.
我是说，我心里有数。

326
00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:56.630
Like, and I know it.
你最好心里有数。

327
00:12:56.810 --> 00:12:57.350
Like, I know.
没错。

328
00:12:57.370 --> 00:12:58.210
You better know it.
非常棒。

329
00:12:58.230 --> 00:12:58.370
Yeah.
而且，你脸上流露出的所有情绪都太惊人了。

330
00:12:58.450 --> 00:12:58.810
Pretty great.
而且不仅你知道，Ken Coapis也知道。

331
00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:04.530
And that, like, everything that comes across your face is just phenomenal.
没错。

332
00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:09.110
And also, not only do you know it, but Ken Coapis knew it, too.
他简直——

333
00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:09.690
Yeah.
大家都知道。

334
00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:11.030
And he's just—
显而易见。

335
00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:12.230
Everyone knew it.
我能告诉你吗？我最近在刷Instagram时，看到有人发帖说，我之所以能有那样的表演，是因为我不知道John会推门进来

336
00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:12.830
It's obvious.
说那句台词？

337
00:13:13.010 --> 00:13:19.150
Can I tell you that I was scrolling Instagram recently and someone posted that the reason
我喜欢他们编造这些东西。

338
00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:24.470
I gave that performance was because I didn't know John was going to come in the door and
但这根本不是真的，各位。

339
00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:25.030
deliver that line?
我知道剧本里有这一段。

340
00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:26.030
I love when they make that stuff up.
那是经过精心设计的。

341
00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:27.630
And it's not true, everybody.
不仅如此，她还必须拍好几次。

342
00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:29.430
I knew it was in the scores.
没错。

343
00:13:29.810 --> 00:13:31.950
Like, it was meticulously timed.
所以说，她知道他要进来。

344
00:13:32.630 --> 00:13:36.430
But not only that, she had to do that take multiple times.
我知道他要进来。

345
00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:36.850
Yeah.
废话。

346
00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:38.670
So it's like, she knew he was coming.
你就是个了不起的演员。

347
00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:39.490
I knew he was coming.
你知道的，大家都爱他。

348
00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:40.090
No s***.
好吧。

349
00:13:40.310 --> 00:13:41.870
You're just an amazing actor.
好吧。

350
00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:44.050
You know, everyone loves him.
好吧。

351
00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:45.410
Of course, he's going to get the job.
当然，他肯定能得到那份工作。

352
00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.650
And, you know, just—we never got the timing right.
而且，你知道，就是——我们总是没能把握好时机。

353
00:13:47.650 --> 00:13:48.590
I shot him down.
我拒绝了他。

354
00:13:48.610 --> 00:13:49.790
He did the same to me.
他也同样拒绝了我。

355
00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:50.830
And—but it's fine.
不过——没关系。

356
00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:54.090
Everything's going to be—and you turn, and there he is.
一切都会——然后你转过身，他就站在那里。

357
00:13:54.170 --> 00:13:55.270
Are you free for dinner tonight?
你今晚有空吃晚饭吗？

358
00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:56.830
You go, yes.
你回答，好的。

359
00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:58.130
And he says, it's a date.
他说，那就约好了。

360
00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:02.850
You turn back to the camera, and your eyes have filled with tears.
你转回镜头前，眼里已经蓄满了泪水。

361
00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:04.110
I don't know how I did it, honestly.
老实说，我不知道我是怎么做到的。

362
00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:05.410
I don't know how you did it either.
我也不知道你是怎么做到的。

363
00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:07.650
Like, how did you do that?
就是说，你是怎么做到的？

364
00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:14.630
Um, when I turned back, the look on Ken Kwapis' face, he was next to the camera.
嗯，当我转过身时，看到肯·夸皮斯（Ken Kwapis）脸上的表情，他就站在摄像机旁边。

365
00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:16.150
He was our director for that episode.
他是那一集的导演。

366
00:14:16.150 --> 00:14:16.810
I remember you saying this.
我记得你说过这个。

367
00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:17.030
Yeah.
是啊。

368
00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:18.470
He looked at me—
他看着我——

369
00:14:18.470 --> 00:14:18.770
It's insane.
太不可思议了。

370
00:14:19.770 --> 00:14:21.690
He'd been with us since the pilot.
他从试播集开始就一直和我们在一起。

371
00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:23.150
He felt like our dad.
他就像我们的父亲一样。

372
00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:23.470
Yeah.
是啊。

373
00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:27.250
And, like, having that moment where your dad is like, you did it, kid.
那种感觉就像，你的父亲对你说，你做到了，孩子。

374
00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:27.510
Yeah.
是啊。

375
00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:31.150
You know when something means something to you, it's really moving?
你知道当某件事对你意义重大时，会让人非常感动吗？

376
00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:31.450
Yeah.
是啊。

377
00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:36.690
But when you can lock eyes with someone who knows just as well what it means to you, then you lose it.
但当你能与一个同样深知这对你意味着什么的人对视时，你就会彻底破防。

378
00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:45.370
And so the fact that the Pam inside of me was getting all of her wishes come true in that moment,
所以，当时我内心深处的帕姆（Pam）所有的愿望都在那一刻成真了，

379
00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:50.390
but then I could look in the eyes of someone else who knew that all of Pam's wishes were coming true,
而我又能看着另一个人的眼睛，他知道帕姆所有的愿望都成真了，

380
00:14:50.810 --> 00:14:51.830
that is what did it.
这才是让我落泪的原因。

381
00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:57.090
If I had to look at a tennis ball, I can't say that you would have gotten the same reaction.
如果当时我必须对着一个网球演，我不敢说你能得到同样的反应。

382
00:14:57.090 --> 00:15:02.270
So there was, like, there was another performance happening off camera that was helping me.
所以当时镜头外还有另一场表演在帮助我。

383
00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:03.810
It's just so amazing.
这真是太神奇了。

384
00:15:03.990 --> 00:15:09.190
And when you did that, I mean, because you had to do multiple takes.
当你那样做的时候，我是说，因为你必须拍好几次。

385
00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:12.490
I don't understand how one can recreate this.
我不明白一个人怎么能重现这种感觉。

386
00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:19.110
Also, because it's not like, you know, a scene where you're starting it out crying.
而且，这不像那种你一开始就在哭的戏。

387
00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:21.590
It's like that's a whole other hard thing.
那是另一件非常困难的事情。

388
00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:29.030
But it's like doing the same scene over and over where you're starting out totally normal and unaffected and then switching over.
但一遍又一遍地演同一场戏，你必须从完全正常、不受影响的状态开始，然后切换情绪，这太难了。

389
00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:30.470
It's just, like, so amazing.
这真是太神奇了。

390
00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:31.990
And I just can't give you enough props.
我真的怎么夸你都不为过。

391
00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:33.290
It's just so magical.
这简直太有魔力了。

392
00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:34.470
And you're so incredible.
你真是太不可思议了。

393
00:15:34.710 --> 00:15:35.150
Thank you.
谢谢你。

394
00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:40.370
I actually think it's easier to do starting to not cry and decrying.
其实我觉得从不哭到哭出来反而更容易。

395
00:15:40.530 --> 00:15:48.890
Because if the writing is right and if you know your character, then the truth of it should make the emotion come.
因为如果剧本写得好，而且你了解你的角色，那么真相本身就应该能引出情感。

396
00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:49.270
Right.
没错。

397
00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:54.830
I've had to do scenes, like, I had to do that scene where I'm just, like, sobbing in the hallway and then Dwight comes up to me.
我以前拍过一些戏，比如我必须演那场在走廊里痛哭，然后德怀特（Dwight）走过来的戏。

398
00:15:55.050 --> 00:16:01.310
It was so much harder to get myself to that state from zero, from nothing.
从零开始让自己进入那种状态要困难得多。

399
00:16:02.150 --> 00:16:02.870
That's crazy.
那太疯狂了。

400
00:16:02.990 --> 00:16:06.850
That's when you have to, like, listen to sad music and, like, all that.
那种时候你就必须得听听悲伤的音乐之类的，做各种准备。

401
00:16:06.870 --> 00:16:09.470
And, like, stay away from everyone between scenes doing bits.
还有，拍戏间隙你就像那样，避开所有人，沉浸在自己的世界里。

402
00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:09.850
Right.
没错。

403
00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:15.130
And I know that everyone kind of left you alone and let you have that to fully get into it.
我知道大家当时都尽量不去打扰你，让你能完全进入状态。

404
00:16:15.210 --> 00:16:17.330
And it's just so amazing and moving.
那真的太棒了，太感人了。

405
00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:28.990
And I'm also obsessed with that your song to get you, I think then, it was the Please, Please, Let Me Get What I Want cover by, who was it, Deftones or something insane?
而且我特别着迷于你选的那首歌，我想当时应该是《Please, Please, Let Me Get What I Want》的翻唱版吧，是谁唱的来着，Deftones 还是什么疯狂的乐队？

406
00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:29.870
I think that's right.
我想应该是吧。

407
00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:30.110
Yeah.
是啊。

408
00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:31.930
That's an insane choice, Jenna.
那真是个疯狂的选择，珍娜。

409
00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:42.690
It's an amazingly insane, amazing, like, by the way, Please, Please, Please, Let Me Get What I Want by The Smiths is an incredible song.
那真是个绝妙又疯狂的选择，顺便说一下，史密斯乐队原版的《Please, Please, Let Me Get What I Want》是一首不可思议的歌。

410
00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:43.850
And it is so heartbreaking.
而且它听起来太让人心碎了。

411
00:16:44.090 --> 00:16:47.670
And when you said that, I thought, wow, that's an amazing choice.
当你提到那首歌时，我想，哇，真是个绝佳的选择。

412
00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:49.370
And I thought, oh, I haven't heard Deftones' version.
我还心想，哦，我还没听过 Deftones 的版本呢。

413
00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:50.550
I listened to it.
我后来去听了。

414
00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:53.790
And it's like, and I'm like, so hard.
听完之后，我整个人都被震撼到了。

415
00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:55.110
Jeff, hell yeah.
杰夫，你说得太对了。

416
00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:58.790
That's just, I love, because music does have that effect.
我真的很喜欢，因为音乐确实有那种感染力。

417
00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:00.590
This one is a metalhead.
这家伙是个金属乐迷。

418
00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:01.470
It's amazing.
太棒了。

419
00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:03.310
My son is.
我儿子也是。

420
00:17:03.310 --> 00:17:09.450
And so, by default, I have now, yeah.
所以受他影响，我现在也听了。

421
00:17:09.450 --> 00:17:09.910
It's amazing.
太神奇了。

422
00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:11.390
It's just so magical.
真的太有魔力了。

423
00:17:11.650 --> 00:17:13.250
And, okay, I'm moving it along, because I have more moments.
好了，我得继续往下说了，因为我还有更多想聊的瞬间。

424
00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:15.350
That was like one and a half-ish of.
刚才那大概算是一个半左右的瞬间吧。

425
00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:16.070
Yeah.
是啊。

426
00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:18.410
It was a lot of moments, I'm just saying, really.
说真的，那其实已经有很多个瞬间了。

427
00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:19.050
Okay, okay.
好吧，好吧。

428
00:17:19.190 --> 00:17:29.450
In my most recent rewatch, because I'm listening to you guys talk about each episode, I'm really watching them more closely now, because now I know so much behind the scenes of it,
最近我重温的时候，因为在听你们聊每一集，所以我现在看得更仔细了，因为我知道了那么多幕后故事，

429
00:17:29.530 --> 00:17:32.110
which is so fun and interesting and exciting.
这真的非常有趣、引人入胜且令人兴奋。

430
00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:39.370
And, Angela, you just are just gold to this show.
而且，安吉拉，你简直是这部剧的瑰宝。

431
00:17:39.550 --> 00:17:45.670
It's just like the amount of times that we watch this show, and I'm like, wait for it.
我们看这部剧看了无数遍，每次我都会想，等着瞧吧。

432
00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:49.430
And then you just say something with the most perfect delivery.
然后你就会用最完美的语调说出那句台词。

433
00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:57.570
And it's so interesting, because I know how different you are from Angela Martin, and how you're not that cold, you know.
这很有趣，因为我知道你本人和安吉拉·马丁有多么不同，你一点都不冷漠，你知道的。

434
00:17:57.690 --> 00:18:00.810
You're this bubbly angel of a person.
你是个活泼开朗、像天使一样的人。

435
00:18:00.810 --> 00:18:09.730
And it is pretty upsetting how incredible you are at playing that kind of a character.
所以你能把那个角色演得那么传神，真的让人感到不可思议。

436
00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:16.470
And I know that you talked about how you've always kind of, before that, played, like, upbeat and fun, light characters.
我知道你之前提到过，在那之前你演的都是那种积极、有趣、轻松的角色。

437
00:18:16.470 --> 00:18:25.650
And, like, on New Girl, you're like, yeah, okay, you know, just this, like, light kind of owly—you have owl eyes, is like what you say in there.
比如在《杰茜驾到》里，你就是那种轻松的、像猫头鹰一样的——你在剧里说你有双猫头鹰眼。

438
00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:27.050
Anyway, moving on.
总之，言归正传。

439
00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:32.550
So I feel like I know you so well now, based on this show.
所以我觉得通过这部剧，我现在非常了解你。

440
00:18:32.910 --> 00:18:36.430
And it's just even more impressive.
这让你显得更加令人印象深刻了。

441
00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:46.690
And, like, okay, specific lines of yours that kill me and that we quote all the time is, like, when Michael is in the bullpen,
还有，有些你的经典台词让我笑得不行，我们经常引用，比如迈克尔在办公区的时候，

442
00:18:46.690 --> 00:18:54.130
and he's trying to kind of derail everyone from knowing that some of them aren't going to get raises or that all the raises are going to be smaller.
他试图转移大家的注意力，不让大家发现有些人拿不到加薪，或者所有人的加薪幅度都会缩水。

443
00:18:54.390 --> 00:18:57.730
And he's like, yes, lend Oscar a cup of sugar.
然后他说，好的，借给奥斯卡一杯糖。

444
00:18:57.750 --> 00:19:00.450
And you go, what are you talking about, Michael?
你回了一句，迈克尔，你在说什么呢？

445
00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:08.050
It's literally, like, the most incredible delivery of a line ever in life.
那简直是我这辈子听过最绝的台词演绎了。

446
00:19:08.050 --> 00:19:12.990
Also, like, the amount of times that you, like, in the conference room, just add, like, an, oh.
还有，你在会议室里，时不时加的那声“哦”。

447
00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:16.450
And it just—it always makes me laugh out loud.
每次都能让我大笑出声。

448
00:19:16.790 --> 00:19:27.110
And your ability to be so cruel is uncanny and unbelievable and so moving.
你那种能把刻薄演得入木三分的能力，简直不可思议，太动人了。

449
00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:36.650
And also, like, just every time, like, Kevin pushes by you and you completely fall, it's just—it kills me.
还有每次凯文撞到你，你整个人摔倒的样子，真的——太搞笑了。

450
00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:40.950
I'm, like, getting flustered, and I'm trying to think of, like, more specific moments.
我都有点语无伦次了，我还在努力回想更多具体的瞬间。

451
00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:42.090
Wait, I have them written down.
等等，我把它们记下来了。

452
00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:42.630
Please.
请说。

453
00:19:42.810 --> 00:19:43.110
Hold on.
稍等。

454
00:19:43.650 --> 00:19:45.290
You mentioned Crime Aid.
你提到了“犯罪援助”。

455
00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:46.750
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

456
00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:47.650
Freaking.
简直是。

457
00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:48.850
Crime Aid.
“犯罪援助”。

458
00:19:49.610 --> 00:19:56.110
I—the—your favorite moment from Crime Aid, I love so much that I asked Matt Beagle and Sam to pull it as a clip.
我——你最喜欢“犯罪援助”里的那个片段，我太喜欢了，所以我让马特·比格尔和萨姆把它剪辑了出来。

459
00:19:56.110 --> 00:19:57.410
If we wanted to hear it.
如果我们想听的话。

460
00:19:57.710 --> 00:20:04.410
Because it's that thing—you love something that we both love is when Michael doesn't know what he's saying, but he's trying to make a point.
因为这就是那种——你喜欢的东西我们也喜欢，就是迈克尔不知道自己在说什么，但他又想表达一个观点的时候。

461
00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:06.850
And he's just meandering all over the place.
他就在那儿东拉西扯，不知所云。

462
00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:10.170
This is one of my favorite Michael moments of all time.
这是我个人有史以来最喜欢的迈克尔时刻之一。

463
00:20:10.370 --> 00:20:13.450
Because Steve Carell, just anything that comes out of his mouth is gold.
因为史蒂夫·卡瑞尔，他嘴里说出来的任何话都是金句。

464
00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:19.110
And really, like, every line of his is my favorite of the entire show.
真的，他说的每一句台词都是我整部剧里最喜欢的。

465
00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:21.310
And specifically, like, what you're saying.
特别是你刚才说的那段。

466
00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:23.770
When he's like, sometimes I just start a sentence.
当他说，有时候我只是开始说一句话。

467
00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:24.190
The deal?
重点呢？

468
00:20:24.210 --> 00:20:25.450
And I just hope I find it.
