那真是太绝了。

630
00:27:14.450 --> 00:27:16.050
It just, oh God.
它简直，天哪。

631
00:27:16.050 --> 00:27:17.710
And it's just so clearly just him.
那简直太有他的风格了。

632
00:27:18.070 --> 00:27:18.270
Yes.
是的。

633
00:27:18.450 --> 00:27:21.250
And it's so exactly how we feel as people.
那正是我们作为普通人的真实感受。

634
00:27:21.510 --> 00:27:26.570
Like, it's just like the most like childlike tantrum flap.
就像是最孩子气的发脾气拍打动作。

635
00:27:26.750 --> 00:27:26.830
Yeah.
是啊。

636
00:27:26.990 --> 00:27:29.610
That just every time he does that, it makes me laugh out loud.
每次他做那个动作，我都会忍不住大笑。

637
00:27:29.810 --> 00:27:34.130
And then also, okay, wait.
还有，好吧，等等。

638
00:27:35.110 --> 00:27:36.530
Jörg, are you dreaming?
约尔格，你在做梦吗？

639
00:27:36.910 --> 00:27:37.530
What's happening?
发生什么事了？

640
00:27:38.250 --> 00:27:38.610
Oh.
噢。

641
00:27:39.130 --> 00:27:39.970
That one got him.
那个戳中他了。

642
00:27:42.010 --> 00:27:45.530
He's looking really pig-like right now, just for everyone wondering.
他现在看起来真的很像猪，告诉大家一声。

643
00:27:45.990 --> 00:27:50.870
The other one was like, just, I mean, prison Mike is just the most iconic thing in the world.
另一个就是，我是说，监狱迈克简直是世界上最标志性的东西。

644
00:27:51.070 --> 00:27:56.910
And also specifically, I love that John in the background is like kind of breaking.
而且我特别喜欢背景里的约翰快要憋不住笑的样子。

645
00:27:56.910 --> 00:28:05.410
But my favorite part of him breaking is I like the idea that it's actually Jim laughing at what Michael is doing.
但我最喜欢他憋笑的部分是，我喜欢这种想法：其实是吉姆在笑迈克的所作所为。

646
00:28:05.630 --> 00:28:14.850
Because one thing that I've always thought about The Office is, of course, the humor at the beginning of Moore is like so dry.
因为我一直觉得《办公室》这部剧，当然，摩尔（Moore）早期的幽默非常冷。

647
00:28:14.850 --> 00:28:17.350
And it's like, no one laughs, right?
就像是，没人会笑，对吧？

648
00:28:17.570 --> 00:28:26.050
And Michael is doing so many things to you, specifically in the first season, that is like, you're just like looking at him deadpan and not laughing.
迈克在第一季里对你做了那么多事，你只是面无表情地看着他，根本笑不出来。

649
00:28:26.290 --> 00:28:38.830
And I feel like the one thing that I've always thought is throughout the show, the amount of things that are so ridiculous and so like unironically funny,
我一直觉得，整部剧里有那么多荒谬且极其好笑的事情，

650
00:28:40.110 --> 00:28:42.610
I would laugh out loud at in real life.
如果是在现实生活中，我肯定会大笑出声。

651
00:28:42.830 --> 00:28:49.490
And like the fact that Jim is dying laughing at Michael doing this prison Mike thing, I think is so real.
吉姆看着迈克尔扮演“监狱迈克”笑得快断气了，我觉得这一点特别真实。

652
00:28:49.850 --> 00:28:53.630
Because wouldn't you laugh at this guy doing that in front of you?
因为如果有人在你面前那样做，你难道不会笑吗？

653
00:28:53.730 --> 00:28:57.250
Like, especially if you're with your friends and you're, you know.
尤其是当你和朋友在一起的时候，你知道的。

654
00:28:57.430 --> 00:28:58.610
And you're not supposed to laugh.
而且你本来不该笑的。

655
00:28:58.610 --> 00:28:59.690
And you're not supposed to laugh.
而且你本来不该笑的。

656
00:29:00.170 --> 00:29:03.890
And so whenever anyone breaks, I'm like, that is so real though.
所以每当有人笑场时，我都会觉得，这太真实了。

657
00:29:03.890 --> 00:29:12.130
Because in real life, somebody doing something as ridiculous as that, you would laugh without even meaning to, even if you're not supposed to.
因为在现实生活中，如果有人做出那么荒唐的事，你就算不想笑也会忍不住笑出来的，哪怕你本来不该笑。

658
00:29:12.290 --> 00:29:14.890
And I love those moments so much.
我太喜欢那些瞬间了。

659
00:29:15.250 --> 00:29:18.050
Anyway, I have to cut myself off because I'm going to keep going.
总之，我得打住，不然我会一直说个没完。

660
00:29:18.250 --> 00:29:18.410
Okay.
好的。

661
00:29:27.710 --> 00:29:30.350
Well, we also want to hear about your movie.
对了，我们也想听听关于你电影的事。

662
00:29:30.490 --> 00:29:30.850
Yes.
好的。

663
00:29:30.970 --> 00:29:31.870
It's coming out.
电影要上映了。

664
00:29:32.050 --> 00:29:33.170
It's a big deal.
这可是件大事。

665
00:29:33.510 --> 00:29:34.790
This is amazing.
太棒了。

666
00:29:35.150 --> 00:29:39.790
Okay, so by the time everyone hears this, the movie will be out because it came out on May 8th.
好的，等大家听到这期节目时，电影应该已经上映了，因为它是5月8号出的。

667
00:29:39.970 --> 00:29:40.230
Yes.
没错。

668
00:29:40.530 --> 00:29:42.050
It's Hit Me Hard and Soft, the tour.
是《Hit Me Hard and Soft》巡演电影。

669
00:29:42.590 --> 00:29:46.690
You co-directed it with James Cameron in 3D.
你和詹姆斯·卡梅隆联合执导了这部3D电影。

670
00:29:46.710 --> 00:29:47.470
It's true.
没错。

671
00:29:48.170 --> 00:29:50.190
I mean, I saw the trailer.
我是说，我看了预告片。

672
00:29:50.470 --> 00:29:51.590
I already have tickets.
我已经买好票了。

673
00:29:51.870 --> 00:29:53.150
I can't wait to see it.
我迫不及待想去看了。

674
00:29:53.270 --> 00:29:54.870
It's part of my daughter's birthday present.
这是我女儿生日礼物的一部分。

675
00:29:54.870 --> 00:29:56.190
I'm taking her on a friend.
我打算带她和一个朋友一起去。

676
00:29:56.370 --> 00:29:56.550
Yes.
太好了。

677
00:29:56.790 --> 00:29:57.330
Oh my God.
天哪。

678
00:29:57.330 --> 00:29:59.610
We've got a whole mom's and daughter's crew.
我们组织了一大群妈妈和女儿。

679
00:29:59.930 --> 00:30:01.530
We'll be filling up two different theaters.
我们要包下两个不同的影厅。

680
00:30:01.890 --> 00:30:02.010
Okay.
好的。

681
00:30:02.410 --> 00:30:03.770
Yeah, tell us about it.
来，跟我们聊聊吧。

682
00:30:03.870 --> 00:30:04.730
It looks so great.
看起来太棒了。

683
00:30:04.850 --> 00:30:07.730
It looks like you're giving people a lot of access too.
看起来你还向观众展示了很多幕后内容。

684
00:30:07.870 --> 00:30:09.070
A little behind the scenes.
一些幕后花絮。

685
00:30:09.070 --> 00:30:12.850
Yeah, that was like not planned and kind of came about naturally.
是的，那其实不是计划好的，是自然而然发生的。

686
00:30:13.270 --> 00:30:16.590
And I at first was very like, no, I don't want to do that.
起初我非常抗拒，心想，不，我不想那样做。

687
00:30:16.710 --> 00:30:22.550
Because I was filmed from when I was 15 to when I was 18 for this documentary that was made.
因为我15岁到18岁时曾被拍过一部纪录片。

688
00:30:22.550 --> 00:30:30.250
Which was an amazing experience, but like a lot of my life was filmed and I kind of have this like, oh no, I'm good.
那是一次很棒的经历，但我的生活被拍了太多，所以我当时有点那种“哦不，我还是算了吧”的感觉。

689
00:30:30.430 --> 00:30:31.990
Like, I don't know if I, you know.
就像是，我不知道我是否……你知道的。

690
00:30:32.150 --> 00:30:37.170
And so when it came about, I was like, oh, I would love to capture this show.
所以当机会来临时，我想，噢，我很想记录下这场演出。

691
00:30:37.330 --> 00:30:39.870
First of all, it's my favorite show I've ever created.
首先，这是我创作过的最喜欢的演出。

692
00:30:40.290 --> 00:30:47.550
And I had such an amazing time on the tour and just in general, that show is like my best work.
我在巡演期间过得非常愉快，总的来说，那场演出是我最好的作品。

693
00:30:47.690 --> 00:30:49.290
Like, I just feel like you in that scene.
就像我刚才说你那个场景一样。

694
00:30:49.410 --> 00:30:50.570
Like, I'm like, yeah, you know what?
我就觉得，没错，你知道吗？

695
00:30:50.650 --> 00:30:51.650
I will agree.
我同意。

696
00:30:51.830 --> 00:30:52.950
This is my best work.
这是我最好的作品。

697
00:30:53.070 --> 00:30:54.030
I feel very proud.
我感到非常自豪。

698
00:30:54.430 --> 00:30:56.270
So I felt really excited about that.
所以我对此感到非常兴奋。

699
00:30:56.370 --> 00:30:59.510
But at first I was like, I don't want to do any behind the scenes stuff.
但起初我确实想过，我不想做任何幕后内容。

700
00:30:59.610 --> 00:31:04.850
I don't want to make it like a documentary of any kind because I don't want to share too much.
我不想把它拍成任何形式的纪录片，因为我不想分享太多个人隐私。

701
00:31:04.850 --> 00:31:11.850
And honestly, Jim, James, Jim, he agreed, by the way.
说实话，吉姆，詹姆斯，吉姆，顺便说一下，他同意了。

702
00:31:11.970 --> 00:31:17.650
But then when we were kind of moving through it, he was like, what if we just like talked and filmed it?
但后来当我们进行到一半时，他说，如果我们只是边聊边拍会怎样？

703
00:31:17.750 --> 00:31:19.650
And I was kind of like, I don't know.
我当时有点犹豫，我说，我不知道。

704
00:31:19.770 --> 00:31:22.210
And it just came so naturally.
结果一切都显得那么自然。

705
00:31:22.450 --> 00:31:30.430
And also beyond being naturally happening, it was also like I saw the importance of it.
而且除了自然发生之外，我也看到了它的重要性。

706
00:31:30.530 --> 00:31:32.150
And I thought, you know what?
我想，你知道吗？

707
00:31:32.150 --> 00:31:36.130
But this is the reality of me and my show.
这就是我和我的演出的真实情况。

708
00:31:36.430 --> 00:31:43.430
And it's like, yeah, if we're going to be showing this show that I've worked so hard on, let's show the experience of doing that.
就像是，没错，既然我们要展示我如此努力准备的这场演出，那就展示一下准备过程中的经历吧。

709
00:31:43.530 --> 00:31:46.890
And what is my day like leading up to it?
我演出前的一天是什么样的？

710
00:31:46.990 --> 00:31:49.770
And also like the fans haven't seen that in a while.
而且粉丝们也有一段时间没看到这些了。

711
00:31:49.770 --> 00:31:52.130
And I thought that it would be really fun for them to.
我觉得这对他们来说会非常有趣。

712
00:31:52.230 --> 00:31:53.170
And also in 3D.
而且还是3D版的。

713
00:31:53.170 --> 00:32:02.830
I mean, I would have loved to have seen my favorite artist when I was young in 3D because I could have felt like I was there and I was in front of them.
我是说，如果我年轻时能看到我最喜欢的艺人的3D演出，我会很开心的，因为那样我就能感觉自己身临其境，就在他们面前一样。

714
00:32:03.030 --> 00:32:11.990
And it's been a really intense and long and grueling process of making it and editing it and working on every aspect of it.
制作、剪辑并打磨每一个细节，这是一个非常紧张、漫长且艰苦的过程。

715
00:32:12.230 --> 00:32:17.750
But it's now I can feel I feel like relieved because it's I feel really good about it.
但现在我感到如释重负，因为我对它感觉非常好。

716
00:32:17.850 --> 00:32:18.830
And I think it's really good.
我觉得它真的很棒。

717
00:32:18.930 --> 00:32:20.530
And I'm really, really excited.
我真的非常非常兴奋。

718
00:32:20.770 --> 00:32:21.610
I can't wait.
我迫不及待了。

719
00:32:21.610 --> 00:32:22.410
Really excited.
真的很兴奋。

720
00:32:22.650 --> 00:32:30.710
You know, there's this great quote that has something to do with like one of the greatest gifts as an artist that you can give other artists is to show your brushstrokes.
你知道，有句名言说，作为艺术家，你能给其他艺术家最好的礼物之一，就是展示你的笔触。

721
00:32:30.830 --> 00:32:31.090
Yeah.
没错。

722
00:32:31.490 --> 00:32:34.730
Because we so often just put out like final.
因为我们通常只是展示最终成品。

723
00:32:35.110 --> 00:32:35.910
You just see the final thing.
你看到的只是最终结果。

724
00:32:36.110 --> 00:32:39.310
And so I feel like with this movie, we're going to get to see some of the brushstrokes.
所以我感觉通过这部电影，我们能看到一些“笔触”。

725
00:32:39.510 --> 00:32:39.650
Yeah.
没错。

726
00:32:39.810 --> 00:32:41.550
We're going to see how the whole thing comes together.
我们将看到整个过程是如何整合在一起的。

727
00:32:41.810 --> 00:32:42.030
Yeah.
没错。

728
00:32:42.250 --> 00:32:45.070
My daughter just admires you so much.
我女儿非常崇拜你。

729
00:32:45.070 --> 00:32:54.750
And I love that she's going to see someone that she idolizes, like doing all the work to get to the big moment on stage.
我很高兴她能看到她偶像为了登上舞台那一刻所付出的所有努力。

730
00:32:54.990 --> 00:32:55.130
Right.
对。

731
00:32:55.530 --> 00:32:56.270
And then also.
而且还有。

732
00:32:56.410 --> 00:32:56.910
Yeah, that's true.
没错，那是真的。

733
00:32:56.970 --> 00:32:57.830
I didn't even think of that.
我甚至都没往那方面想。

734
00:32:57.830 --> 00:32:58.890
It's just really cool.
这真的很酷。

735
00:32:58.890 --> 00:33:01.990
You know, it's like a really valuable gift that you're giving.
你知道，这就像是你给予的一份非常有价值的礼物。

736
00:33:02.190 --> 00:33:02.310
Yeah.
没错。

737
00:33:02.450 --> 00:33:03.090
So thank you.
所以谢谢你。

738
00:33:03.270 --> 00:33:04.930
I mean, I always love the final product.
我是说，我总是喜欢最终的产品。

739
00:33:04.930 --> 00:33:11.450
The process is what always just like tugs at my heartstrings because you see how much work it really is.
但过程总是最触动我的心弦，因为你能看到它背后付出了多少努力。

740
00:33:11.590 --> 00:33:14.870
And it's so important to see the work that you put into something.
看到你为某件事所投入的努力是非常重要的。

741
00:33:15.070 --> 00:33:15.470
That's really true.
确实如此。

742
00:33:15.670 --> 00:33:15.850
Yeah.
没错。

743
00:33:15.870 --> 00:33:16.910
Yeah, that's really true.
没错，确实如此。

744
00:33:17.070 --> 00:33:18.470
I hadn't really thought about that.
我之前真的没想过这一点。

745
00:33:18.590 --> 00:33:25.050
And it's really true because I think like it's so easy to see a final product and be like, well, that was perfect from the start.
这确实是真的，因为我觉得人们很容易看到最终成品，然后觉得，嗯，它从一开始就是完美的。

746
00:33:25.190 --> 00:33:25.870
And it just wasn't.
但事实并非如此。

747
00:33:25.870 --> 00:33:34.550
And also, like, you know, even though this movie, we didn't start it until I was already way into the tour and, you know,
而且，你知道，尽管这部电影，我们直到巡演进行到一半才开始拍摄，而且，你知道，

748
00:33:34.730 --> 00:33:40.850
I had been doing the show for a while and it was kind of perfect at that point in terms of like process.
那时我已经演了一段时间了，就过程而言，它已经相当完美了。

749
00:33:41.890 --> 00:33:54.530
But we had filmed like, just to have, we'd filmed a little bit of the beginning of the tour and also specifically like the night before, and it's in the movie somewhat,
但我们确实拍了一些素材，只是为了留存，我们拍了一点巡演开始时的片段，还有特别是在前一天晚上，电影里也有一部分，

750
00:33:54.730 --> 00:34:00.490
but the night before we started filming, I sprained my ankle, which I hadn't done in six years.
但在我们开始拍摄的前一天晚上，我扭伤了脚踝，这可是我六年来第一次。

751
00:34:00.490 --> 00:34:01.670
I used to do all the time.
我以前经常这么做。

752
00:34:01.930 --> 00:34:05.050
And literally, I was in Manchester to film the movie.
当时我确实在曼彻斯特拍电影。

753
00:34:05.210 --> 00:34:06.250
I had this meeting with Jim.
我和吉姆有个会面。

754
00:34:06.250 --> 00:34:12.450
I went to my hotel and I immediately sprained my ankle by stepping out onto my balcony, which was a two inch drop.
我回到酒店，刚踏上阳台就扭伤了脚踝，那儿其实只有两英寸高。

755
00:34:12.450 --> 00:34:17.270
And you're so athletic in your concerts, but it was like stepping on the balcony.
你在演唱会上那么有活力，结果却是在阳台上摔的。

756
00:34:17.470 --> 00:34:18.330
Yes, that's what did it.
没错，就是这么弄伤的。

757
00:34:18.470 --> 00:34:26.050
And so I, the next day, started one of many, many shows in a row being filmed in 3D with a sprained ankle.
第二天，我就带着扭伤的脚踝，开始了连续多场3D电影的拍摄。

758
00:34:26.070 --> 00:34:27.070
And I was like, you know what?
当时我就想，你知道吗？

759
00:34:27.170 --> 00:34:28.190
This gives me a challenge.
这对我来说是个挑战。

760
00:34:28.190 --> 00:34:29.090
I love a challenge.
我喜欢挑战。

761
00:34:29.330 --> 00:34:30.010
I'm going to do it.
我一定要做到。

762
00:34:30.090 --> 00:34:31.110
I'm going to, you know.
我打算，你知道的。

763
00:34:31.110 --> 00:34:44.630
And I think like really what the movie is about, aside from, you know, the fact that this tour and this show is so special for me and I want everyone to see it.
我觉得这部电影真正的主题，除了这次巡演和演出对我意义非凡、我希望每个人都能看到之外，

764
00:34:44.630 --> 00:34:50.810
And the fact that the tour ended and not everyone in the entire world got to watch it is,
考虑到巡演已经结束，并非全世界的人都有机会观看，

765
00:34:51.030 --> 00:34:58.270
I feel so grateful and lucky that people who didn't get to come are going to get to see it and feel like they were there.
我感到非常感激和幸运，那些没能到场的人也能看到它，并感受到身临其境的体验。

766
00:34:58.430 --> 00:35:01.450
Also, people who did get to see it and want to relive it.
当然，还有那些看过演出、想要重温的人。

767
00:35:01.630 --> 00:35:09.850
And specifically, selfishly, that I will forever get to watch this and ask this.
而且私心地说，我以后也能随时观看并回味这一切。

768
00:35:09.850 --> 00:35:16.010
Yes, it's so special, I think, to have any kind of visual or oral history of something that meant a lot to you.
是的，我觉得能为对自己意义重大的事情留下影像或口述历史，真的非常特别。

769
00:35:16.250 --> 00:35:18.130
And we have that with our podcaSt.
我们做播客也是这样。

770
00:35:18.330 --> 00:35:19.810
We think about that all the time.
我们一直都在想这个问题。

771
00:35:19.970 --> 00:35:20.090
Yeah.
没错。

772
00:35:20.310 --> 00:35:28.910
Yeah, we've said now, we've gotten on record, every memory and story, minus the ones we're saving for Office Ladies Burn It to the Ground.
是啊，我们现在已经把所有的回忆和故事都记录下来了，除了那些我们留着要在《办公室女士：彻底摧毁》里讲的。

773
00:35:29.050 --> 00:35:29.210
Yeah.
没错。

774
00:35:29.410 --> 00:35:30.790
We have them out there now.
我们现在把它们都公开了。

775
00:35:30.890 --> 00:35:32.190
Girl, we're all ready for that one.
天哪，我们都准备好听那一期了。

776
00:35:32.410 --> 00:35:34.610
We are all ready for that.
我们都准备好了。

777
00:35:35.010 --> 00:35:43.170
But it's like, literally, in the office, when Phyllis says, like, I worked here for this long and I never wrote anything down.
但这就像《办公室》里菲利斯说的那样，我在这里工作了这么久，却从来没写下过什么。

778
00:35:43.470 --> 00:35:45.930
You know, we all think, like, oh, I'll remember that forever.
你知道，我们都以为自己会永远记得。

779
00:35:45.930 --> 00:35:46.270
Yeah.
是啊。

780
00:35:46.350 --> 00:35:47.350
And you just won't.
但你根本记不住。

781
00:35:47.490 --> 00:35:52.510
And, like, if it's filmed, and, like, you guys, like, this is recorded forever.
如果被拍下来了，就像你们这样，这会被永远记录下来。

782
00:35:52.570 --> 00:35:56.590
Like, you're going to have this forever to listen to and you have the office forever to watch.
你们以后可以永远听这些录音，也可以永远看《办公室》。

783
00:35:56.590 --> 00:35:58.250
Like, it's just such a gift.
这真是一份大礼。

784
00:35:58.410 --> 00:36:05.610
And I feel, honestly, before Jim reached out to us, me, through my mother, he sent an email to my mom.
老实说，在吉姆通过我母亲联系我之前，他先给我妈发了封邮件。

785
00:36:05.790 --> 00:36:06.710
Literally, that's how it happened.
真的，事情就是这样发生的。

786
00:36:07.450 --> 00:36:14.770
I was like, I didn't have any plans to film the show because I wasn't going to make a concert film of any kind.
当时我根本没打算拍这场演出，因为我没想过要制作任何形式的演唱会电影。

787
00:36:14.970 --> 00:36:18.310
And I was already feeling like, damn, that sucks.
我当时已经在想，该死，这太糟糕了。

788
00:36:18.310 --> 00:36:24.310
Like, this is such an important show to me and no one's ever going to be able to, like, watch it.
这场演出对我如此重要，却没人能看到。

789
00:36:24.450 --> 00:36:27.810
And the movie really is about the fans.
所以这部电影真的是为了粉丝而拍的。

790
00:36:27.970 --> 00:36:40.150
Like, the real truth is that it's all about the fans and my feeling of devotion to them and their feeling of that with me and our love.
事实就是，这一切都是为了粉丝，为了我对他们的那份深情，以及他们对我的回应，还有我们之间的爱。

791
00:36:40.310 --> 00:36:42.310
And, like, honestly, similar to The Office.
老实说，这和《办公室》很像。

792
00:36:42.310 --> 00:36:45.750
It's like, what am I without my fans, you know?
就像如果没有粉丝，我算什么呢？

793
00:36:45.930 --> 00:36:47.910
And it's like, what is The Office without the fans?
如果没有粉丝，《办公室》又算什么呢？

794
00:36:47.910 --> 00:36:50.070
It's just, it's all this one big—
这只是，这一切都是一个巨大的——

795
00:36:50.070 --> 00:36:51.110
Absolutely, the community.
没错，就是那种社区感。

796
00:36:51.270 --> 00:36:52.270
The community of it.
那种社区氛围。

797
00:36:52.350 --> 00:36:53.830
And that's my favorite thing in the world.
那是我世界上最喜欢的东西。

798
00:36:53.850 --> 00:36:55.950
I wouldn't do any of this if it weren't for that, you know?
如果不是因为这个，我根本不会做这些，你懂吗？

799
00:36:56.370 --> 00:36:59.170
It's a really cool thing.
这真的很酷。

800
00:36:59.170 --> 00:37:03.250
The openness and the, like, human-to-human thing that happens.
那种开放性，以及人与人之间产生的共鸣。

801
00:37:03.550 --> 00:37:08.030
Like, when we meet someone and they are telling us how much The Office means to them,
比如，当我们遇到一些人，他们告诉我们《办公室》这部剧对他们有多重要时，

802
00:37:08.170 --> 00:37:16.150
that is such a gift to me that I get to be part of this thing that brought that other person this joy or whatever.
能参与到这部给他人带来快乐的作品中，对我来说真是一份礼物。

803
00:37:16.150 --> 00:37:18.970
So, it's, like, it's such a really cool connection.
所以，这真的是一种非常棒的联结。

804
00:37:19.270 --> 00:37:19.450
Yeah.
是啊。

805
00:37:19.450 --> 00:37:20.150
It's really cool.
真的很棒。

806
00:37:20.350 --> 00:37:29.050
And, like, you know, this is, like, I know, like, an intense subject, but, like, what you were saying about sharing your process,
而且，我知道这可能是一个比较沉重的话题，但关于你刚才提到的分享创作过程，

807
00:37:29.510 --> 00:37:42.610
that made me think of, like, your health journey, Jenna, and how what you said on the podcast about, like, this is a really intense, scary thing to be going through.
让我想到了你的健康之旅，Jenna。你在播客里说过，经历这些是非常沉重且可怕的事情。

808
00:37:42.610 --> 00:37:48.230
And you have totally the right to be, like, I'm never speaking about it.
你完全有权利说：我绝不会谈论这件事。

809
00:37:48.370 --> 00:37:49.910
I'm never talking about it.
我绝不会提起它。

810
00:37:50.090 --> 00:37:51.670
Please don't ask me about it.
请不要问我关于它的事。

811
00:37:51.670 --> 00:38:02.650
And instead, because you have said on this podcast about how, like, sharing your experience might help other people and other people who are experiencing this.
但相反，正如你在播客中所说，分享你的经历可能会帮助到其他正在经历同样困境的人。

812
00:38:02.830 --> 00:38:06.370
And that is such an amazing gift.
那真是一份了不起的礼物。

813
00:38:06.390 --> 00:38:16.590
And the amount of people that I think you sharing your health journey with, like, changed their lives and made them feel seen and, like, they're not alone.
我想，你分享自己的健康之旅改变了许多人的生活，让他们感到被理解，让他们觉得不再孤单。

814
00:38:16.590 --> 00:38:18.030
And that's just really special.
那真的非常特别。

815
00:38:18.150 --> 00:38:19.150
And you don't have to do that.
你本不必这样做。

816
00:38:19.350 --> 00:38:19.830
Yet, you do.
但你还是做了。

817
00:38:20.030 --> 00:38:25.230
And I think, like, that's obviously, like, completely a different thing than this stupid little movie I'm doing.
我觉得这显然和我正在拍的那部小破电影完全是两码事。

818
00:38:25.490 --> 00:38:25.710
Oh, no, no.
噢，不，不。

819
00:38:25.750 --> 00:38:27.350
But it just made me think of that.
但这确实让我想到了这一点。

820
00:38:27.450 --> 00:38:31.570
And I just wanted to verbalize to you, like, you don't owe anyone anything.
我只是想亲口告诉你，你不欠任何人什么。

821
00:38:32.190 --> 00:38:34.230
And yet, you're so giving.
然而，你却如此慷慨。

822
00:38:34.370 --> 00:38:35.870
And it's just so magical.
这真是太神奇了。

823
00:38:35.870 --> 00:38:43.110
And, like, sharing your story with people just to help them is so selfless and so kind.
为了帮助他人而分享你的故事，这非常无私，也非常善良。

824
00:38:43.430 --> 00:38:45.150
And, yeah, I just had to say that.
所以，是的，我必须得说出来。

825
00:38:45.150 --> 00:38:46.550
Well, thank you.
嗯，谢谢你。

826
00:38:46.890 --> 00:38:48.630
You know, it is a fine line.
你知道，这中间有一条微妙的界限。

827
00:38:48.810 --> 00:38:54.610
It's like there's always that question of how much do I share and how much do I keep for myself?
就像总会面临这样的问题：我该分享多少，又该为自己保留多少？

828
00:38:54.990 --> 00:39:00.730
Sometimes, you know, when I start sharing about breast cancer, I have to think about breast cancer.
有时候，你知道，当我开始谈论乳腺癌时，我就不得不去想乳腺癌这件事。

829
00:39:01.130 --> 00:39:03.870
And I'm pretty excited to not think about it.
而我其实很想不去想它。

830
00:39:05.230 --> 00:39:06.450
So there's that.
所以情况就是这样。

831
00:39:06.450 --> 00:39:08.590
But the thing is,
但关键在于，

832
00:39:08.650 --> 00:39:23.350
is that any time I've had a person tell me that they got checked because they heard my story or they found something early enough to do something about it because they got checked because they heard my story,
每当有人告诉我，因为听了我的故事他们去做了检查，或者因为听了我的故事他们及时发现问题并采取了行动，

833
00:39:23.710 --> 00:39:25.550
it means so much to me.
这对我来说意义重大。

834
00:39:25.550 --> 00:39:27.690
Like, it means so much to me.
真的，意义非凡。

835
00:39:27.810 --> 00:39:31.750
But yet, even still, I do pick my moments.
但即便如此，我还是会选择合适的时机。

836
00:39:31.770 --> 00:39:35.710
And I think that it's okay to pick your moments of access.
我认为选择分享的时机是可以的。

837
00:39:36.010 --> 00:39:37.170
Like, you don't have to give everything.
你不需要把一切都和盘托出。

838
00:39:37.590 --> 00:39:41.330
But, you know, there's a balance there.
但你知道，这中间需要一种平衡。

839
00:39:41.330 --> 00:39:49.270
And I think that's, as an artist, I think we're always trying to find that balance, which is, like, how much do I have to keep for myself?
作为艺术家，我觉得我们总是在寻找那种平衡，也就是：我该为自己保留多少？

840
00:39:49.350 --> 00:39:57.910
Also, in order to do my art, I don't know about you, but, like, there's a certain amount of, like, process that I get into superstitious thinking.
另外，为了进行创作，我不知道你怎么样，但我确实会陷入某种迷信般的思维过程。

841
00:39:58.090 --> 00:40:00.770
And if I share too much, then it doesn't work.
如果我分享得太多，事情反而就不灵了。

842
00:40:00.770 --> 00:40:09.250
Yeah, and also, like, again, that just what you were saying made me think of how much I look up to you and how much everyone looks up to you.
是啊，而且再次回到你刚才说的话，这让我想到我有多么敬仰你，大家又有多么敬仰你。

843
00:40:09.250 --> 00:40:15.990
And I'm in no way trying to compare it the two or your experience and your journey with anything in the entire world because it's, like—
我绝不是要把这两者，或者说你的经历与世界上任何其他事情相提并论，因为这——

844
00:40:15.990 --> 00:40:17.410
But you're talking about sharing.
但你是在谈论分享。

845
00:40:17.570 --> 00:40:18.510
But I'm just talking about in general.
我只是在泛泛而谈。

846
00:40:18.670 --> 00:40:19.630
No, when you get—
不，当你——

847
00:40:19.630 --> 00:40:20.950
Sharing is so—
分享是如此——

848
00:40:20.950 --> 00:40:22.450
Sharing, you put yourself out there.
分享，意味着你把自己展现给世界。

849
00:40:22.590 --> 00:40:23.610
Yeah, that's what I'm saying.
对，我说的就是这个。

850
00:40:23.890 --> 00:40:30.430
And every time you share, no matter what it is you're sharing, and in life, whether you're, like,
无论你分享的是什么，每一次分享，在生活中，无论你是在，比如，

851
00:40:30.770 --> 00:40:39.930
a junior in high school and you decide to share your essay in front of the class or you're, I don't know, a nurse at the hospital and you share, like, the crochet sweater you made.
你是一名高中三年级学生，决定在全班面前分享你的作文，或者你是一名医院护士，分享了你亲手钩织的毛衣。

852
00:40:40.090 --> 00:40:40.570
I don't know.
我不知道。

853
00:40:40.790 --> 00:40:42.650
Anyway, this is, like, a Michael Scott analogy.
总之，这就像是一个迈克尔·斯科特式的类比。

854
00:40:42.650 --> 00:40:45.070
I am turning into Michael Scott, we've discovered.
我们发现，我正在变成迈克尔·斯科特。

855
00:40:45.370 --> 00:40:49.870
But I do think every time you share as a person, you're stepping out there.
但我确实认为，每当你以个人的身份进行分享时，你都是在迈出那一步。

856
00:40:50.070 --> 00:40:50.210
Rewarded.
得到回报。

857
00:40:50.470 --> 00:40:50.790
Yeah.
是啊。

858
00:40:51.030 --> 00:40:56.350
And it's, like, it's just—we must not forget that sharing saves lives.
而且，这就像是——我们绝不能忘记，分享可以拯救生命。

859
00:40:56.470 --> 00:40:56.650
Yes.
没错。

860
00:41:00.670 --> 00:41:01.590
Uh, no.
呃，不。

861
00:41:01.930 --> 00:41:02.290
No.
不。

862
00:41:02.490 --> 00:41:03.030
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

863
00:41:03.130 --> 00:41:04.290
You don't have to, also.
你其实不必非要这么做。

864
00:41:04.490 --> 00:41:05.190
You don't ever have to.
你永远不必非要这么做。

865
00:41:05.310 --> 00:41:05.990
You don't have to.
你没必要这么做。

866
00:41:06.090 --> 00:41:06.930
You get to decide.
决定权在你手中。

867
00:41:07.170 --> 00:41:13.690
And the one thing I will say, you know, about The Office and about your concerts and going to concerts like that,
关于《办公室》以及你的演唱会，还有去参加那样的演唱会，我想说的一点是，

868
00:41:13.770 --> 00:41:18.730
my daughter went to this concert with her friends and saw it, and there is a shared joy.
我女儿和朋友们去看了那场演唱会，那是一种共享的快乐。

869
00:41:19.270 --> 00:41:20.610
And that's amazing.
那真的很棒。

870
00:41:20.790 --> 00:41:20.990
Yeah.
是啊。

871
00:41:21.170 --> 00:41:25.630
Like, to share joy with someone, like, that should be our goal, right?
就像，与人分享快乐，这应该是我们的目标，对吧？

872
00:41:25.630 --> 00:41:29.730
It's to share joy, and I know your movie's going to do that for people.
就是分享快乐，我知道你的电影也会为人们带来这一点。

873
00:41:29.970 --> 00:41:30.950
Oh, thanks, Angela.
噢，谢谢你，安吉拉。

874
00:41:31.290 --> 00:41:34.330
And it's going to bring it to people who didn't get a chance to see it.
它会把这份快乐带给那些没机会看现场的人。

875
00:41:34.470 --> 00:41:34.730
Who didn't get to see it.
那些没能看到的人。

876
00:41:34.730 --> 00:41:35.130
I know.
我知道。

877
00:41:35.170 --> 00:41:35.490
Yeah.
是啊。

878
00:41:35.490 --> 00:41:39.170
That, to me, is, like, the most important thing, you know?
对我来说，那才是最重要的事，你懂吗？

879
00:41:39.410 --> 00:41:39.550
Yeah.
是啊。

880
00:41:39.550 --> 00:41:40.870
And I'm just really excited.
我真的感到很兴奋。

881
00:41:41.030 --> 00:41:47.430
And also, I'm just—I'm excited, again, like what you said, like, for people to, like, go have that experience together.
而且，就像你刚才说的，我很高兴人们能一起去获得那种体验。

882
00:41:47.430 --> 00:41:52.530
And, like, go with their friends and make friends and have this memory and go with their families.
和朋友们一起去，结交新朋友，留下这段回忆，或者和家人一起去。

883
00:41:52.850 --> 00:41:56.130
And, you know, it's just, like, thinking about that is really, really special.
你知道，想到这些真的非常、非常特别。

884
00:41:56.590 --> 00:42:05.510
Anyway, sorry, Jenna, to bring that stuff up, but I just wanted to say that I feel very inspired by you and very tender towards you.
总之，抱歉，珍娜，提起这些事，但我只是想说，我从你身上感到非常受鼓舞，也对你怀有很深的情谊。

885
00:42:05.910 --> 00:42:07.590
Well, I actually appreciate you saying it.
嗯，我真的很感激你这么说。

886
00:42:07.710 --> 00:42:14.570
It was well-timed because I just agreed to do a little bit of, like, a public service campaign, and I was feeling a little nervous about it.
你说得正是时候，因为我刚答应参加一个公益宣传活动，心里还有点紧张。

887
00:42:14.750 --> 00:42:15.050
You were.
你确实是。

888
00:42:15.190 --> 00:42:15.490
Wow.
哇。

889
00:42:15.870 --> 00:42:16.710
That's a lot.
那可不简单。

890
00:42:16.710 --> 00:42:20.290
So, thank you, because, you know, I was nervous.
所以，谢谢你，因为我之前确实很紧张。

891
00:42:20.530 --> 00:42:23.630
So, I'm going to go into this campaign, and I'm going to be fired up.
现在，我要去参加这个活动了，我会充满干劲的。

892
00:42:23.630 --> 00:42:24.290
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

893
00:42:24.430 --> 00:42:25.330
Thanks to you.
多亏了你。

894
00:42:25.590 --> 00:42:26.350
Oh, God.
天呐。

895
00:42:26.670 --> 00:42:27.310
I'm glad.
我很高兴。

896
00:42:27.570 --> 00:42:28.150
You're amazing.
你太棒了。

897
00:42:28.830 --> 00:42:29.750
Everyone loves you.
大家都爱你。

898
00:42:29.910 --> 00:42:30.170
Anyway.
总之。

899
00:42:30.530 --> 00:42:30.870
All right.
好吧。

900
00:42:30.970 --> 00:42:31.350
Well, listen.
那么，听着。

901
00:42:31.650 --> 00:42:36.050
We have one more thing planned before you leave, which is that you have requested—
在你离开之前，我们还安排了一件事，就是你之前要求的——

902
00:42:36.050 --> 00:42:37.090
Yes, I have.
是的，我要求过。

903
00:42:37.190 --> 00:42:38.430
—to do an office quiz.
——做一个《办公室》问答测试。

904
00:42:38.570 --> 00:42:39.150
With your friend, Jack.
和你朋友杰克一起。

905
00:42:39.150 --> 00:42:40.470
With my friend, Jack.
和我朋友杰克一起。

906
00:42:40.630 --> 00:42:40.810
Okay.
好的。

907
00:42:40.810 --> 00:42:42.490
So, let me explain really quick.
那么，我快速解释一下。

908
00:42:42.490 --> 00:42:46.490
So, my best friend, Alex Wolfe.
我最好的朋友是亚历克斯·沃尔夫。

909
00:42:46.490 --> 00:42:47.270
He's an incredible actor.
他是一位了不起的演员。

910
00:42:47.310 --> 00:42:47.790
He's wonderful.
他非常棒。

911
00:42:48.270 --> 00:42:52.030
And Alex, he has another very best friend.
而亚历克斯还有另一位挚友。

912
00:42:52.030 --> 00:42:54.070
And it's Jack Metzger.
就是杰克·梅茨格。

913
00:42:54.310 --> 00:42:59.230
